{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>According to all that… et Moshe.</b> And it was not sufficient to say ״אוֹתוֹ״ — though it would be understood that he is speaking about Moshe — in order to alert you that this is an independent statement, being the words of Torah itself that testify and declare that the command from Him to them was ״כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר צִוָּה ה׳ אֶת מֹשֶׁה״ — something that would not have been heard if it had said ״אוֹתוֹ״, for then it would have been heard as the conclusion of the statement ״וַיֹּאמֶר מֹשֶׁה וְגוֹ׳ כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר צִוָּה ה׳ אוֹתוֹ״, and one could still say that he merely thought thus, and who is to say that he did not err in his words or alter [them] in a lapse of attention." "<b>Thus is concluded the pericah of Pinchas.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:15:52.492998838Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}